WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.990
If you've seen the trailer for Avengers: Endgame,
then you've gotten a glimpse of Clint Barton's

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.500
return.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.280
But the man previously known as Hawkeye is
very likely returning to the MCU with a whole

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.720
new codename: Ronin.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.020
If you're wondering what the deal is with
this mysterious new persona, you're probably

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.720
not alone.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.600
Let's break down the history of this Marvel
Comics samurai.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.919
Clint Barton isn't the first Marvel Comics
character to wear the mask of Ronin.

00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:28.979
While the Ronin identity wouldn't appear in
comic books until 2005, the first character

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.820
to wear the costume debuted in 1999.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.140
Her name was Maya Lopez, also known as Echo,
and she made her first appearance in the pages

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.620
of Daredevil #9.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.800
Though Maya is deaf, she has the ability to
exactly mimic any action she's ever seen,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.820
from Jackie Chan's stunts to Liberace's piano
playing.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:51.129
When she met Matt Murdock, better known as
Daredevil, the attraction was immediate, and

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:52.680
the two promptly fell in love.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.920
Unfortunately, like many of Matt Murdock's
relationships, this romance didn't end well.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:03.059
Maya was manipulated by the Kingpin into believing
that Daredevil had killed her father, a mind-game

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.480
that convinced her to try and kill the vigilante.

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:09.520
She soon found out that the Kingpin himself
was the one who killed her father, so she

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.440
shot him in the face and then vanished…
for a while.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.180
"But if there's a stunning woman with questionable
character in the room, Matt Murdock’s gonna

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.270
find her, and Foggy Nelson is gonna suffer.”

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.280
"I don't disagree with anything you're saying."

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.420
Ronin's first outing came in the pages of
New Avengers, during a battle against Hydra,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.759
the Hand, and the Yakuza-affiliated Yashida
clan.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:34.340
Captain America recruited the mysterious fighter
onto the Avengers, thanks to a reference from

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:34.980
Daredevil.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.440
During Ronin's first appearance, her real
identity was kept a mystery, with readers

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.100
left to puzzle out just who this new hero
was.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.180
With a loose-fitting costume featuring a full
face mask, it could've been anyone.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.340
The mystery established that Ronin wasn't
just a new superhero - it was an identity

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.369
that any Marvel character could use for covert
purposes, with several unexpected heroes wearing

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:56.720
the mask in the years to come.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.640
The 2004 story arc "Avengers Disassembled"
resulted in the apparent deaths of multiple

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.920
Avengers, including Scott Lang, the Vision,
and Hawkeye.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.240
But death is rarely a permanent condition
in comic books, with Hawkeye returning to

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.520
life thanks to the reality-altering powers
of the Scarlet Witch.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.820
"None of this makes sense."

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.580
When Clint came back to life, he had trouble
returning to his work as Hawkeye, partly because

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.140
a new hero, Kate Bishop, had taken on the
Hawkeye name for herself as a member of the

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.080
Young Avengers.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.580
While everyone would eventually agree that
the world was just fine with two Hawkeyes,

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.140
Clint didn't feel that way at first.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.580
Before taking up his old name again, he also
did a stretch as Ronin.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:39.740
After Clint met the first Ronin during a rescue
mission, she passed the costume on to him,

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.540
explaining that the identity had served its
purpose for her.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.040
It was his to use, for as long as he needed
it.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.720
Clint reverted to his Hawkeye identity in
2010, when the Avengers reformed after the

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.020
events of "Civil War."

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:55.480
While this marked the end of Clint's tenure
as the hero, it was not the end of Ronin.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.840
The next time Ronin showed up was during the "Widowmaker" crossover in 2010.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.420
The Black Widow-centric story kicked off with
the murder of several Russian spies by a group

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.360
led by Ronin.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.680
When a team of Russian superheroes tried to
arrest Hawkeye for the killings, everyone

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.040
soon realized that someone else was wearing
the mask.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.280
This new Ronin was the leader of a criminal
group called the Dark Ocean Society.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:22.000
This time, Ronin's real identity was Alexi
Shostakov, also known as the first Red Guardian.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:26.600
That character can be seen as the Soviet Union's
answer to Captain America - and he was also

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.000
the Black Widow's ex-husband.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.560
His plan as Ronin was to use the Dark Ocean
Society to restore Russia to its former Soviet

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.780
glory, but the heroes were able to take him
down.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.040
They also apparently took the Ronin costume
back home with them, putting it in a box for

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.800
a couple years at Avengers HQ.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.180
Maybe they just thought it looked cool - or
maybe they thought it could come in handy

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:45.680
later.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.760
"Nice outfit."

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:54.680
When the Mighty Avengers series relaunched
in 2013, they were accompanied by a new, mysterious

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.180
hero.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:04:00.080
This fighter kept his identity secret to avoid
attention from his enemies, the mysterious

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:00.740
"Deathwalkers."

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:06.260
So he grabbed the first costume that was available:
a neon green-and-pink bootleg Spider-Man costume

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.500
with "SPIDER HERO" written on the chest.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.800
Spider Hero was a confusing character, both
for comic book readers and the character's

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.460
teammates.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.380
Unlike other Spider-People, he didn't climb
walls or shoot webs, and instead he beat up

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:23.200
bad guys with a pair of nunchuks, basically
behaving more like a ninja-turtle than a spider-man.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.040
Making things more mysterious, he also seemed
to have some knowledge of the mystical arts.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.020
The Spider Hero costume didn't last too long
in the series.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.520
By the fourth issue, the mysterious good guy
was gifted the Ronin costume, to help keep

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.920
his identity a secret in a slightly more professional
looking way.

00:04:39.129 --> 00:04:43.740
Finally, in Mighty Avengers #9, the identity
of this masked man was revealed.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.400
He was none other than Eric Brooks - better
known to most audiences as the vampire slayer

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.000
Blade.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.140
"You gotta be kidding me."

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:56.259
The Endgame trailer finally answers the question
of what Clint Barton has been up to since

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.460
the events of Captain America: Civil War.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.900
His outfit sure seems to look like the Ronin
costume, but what inspired him to take up

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:03.420
the sword?

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.460
We have an idea, but it's not a pleasant one.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.139
Avengers: Age of Ultron showed us that Hawkeye
had a whole life outside of his work as a

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.420
covert operative, with a beautiful family
on a peaceful farm.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.080
After he was arrested at the end of Civil
War, he retired to be with his wife and children,

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.759
sitting out Infinity War - until Thanos won.

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:26.100
It seems very likely that Clint's family was
a part of the 50 percent of life that Thanos

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.860
decimated, meaning that Clint had to watch
them fade away into dust.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:33.980
The horror of that seems like more than enough
to inspire Clint to take on a darker identity,

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.530
go to another country, and start stabbing
people.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.499
Could he succeed in beating Thanos where the
others failed?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.699
Well, it's worth a shot.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.600
"Just can't seem to miss."

